WEBVTT

00:17.330 --> 00:18.830
GHOST BUSTERZ!

00:17.710 --> 00:20.460
OH! The time has come

00:18.250 --> 00:18.830
BUSTERZ!

00:20.460 --> 00:23.840
To stand up for tomorrow

00:22.790 --> 00:24.250
OH OH OH!

00:23.840 --> 00:26.420
We're ghostbusterz

00:26.420 --> 00:31.050
Breakin' away from the old ghosts

00:31.050 --> 00:34.430
Of history

00:34.430 --> 00:37.810
Breaking free!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

01:13.300 --> 01:17.100
No fear for anything in our way!

01:15.630 --> 01:20.430
Presented by hwat fansubs

01:17.100 --> 01:18.640
The time has come

01:33.030 --> 01:37.250
The seventh month of 1600 AD, or Keicho 5.

01:37.610 --> 01:41.410
Charging Tokugawa Ieyasu with thirteen articles of impeachment,

01:41.410 --> 01:48.320
Ishida Mitsunari sent messengers to various daimyo in the name of the Toyotomi clan,

01:48.320 --> 01:51.500
telling them to raise armies.

01:51.500 --> 01:56.600
At the same time, beings seeking to end the period of turbulence

01:56.600 --> 02:00.460
and build a kingdom to last a thousand years

02:00.460 --> 02:04.710
were about to awaken from a thousand-year sleep.

02:04.710 --> 02:06.750
And then...

02:06.750 --> 02:10.480
On the fifteenth day of the ninth month, at Sekigahara,

02:10.480 --> 02:12.950
the Eastern Army of Tokugawa Ieyasu clashed with

02:12.950 --> 02:18.080
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and Ishida Mitsunari.

02:18.080 --> 02:21.550
As a result of the performance of Kobayakawa Hideaki's troops,

02:21.550 --> 02:27.460
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and
Ishida Mitsunari achieved a sweeping victory,

02:27.460 --> 02:33.710
bringing what should have been
three hundred years of peace to the world.

02:34.570 --> 02:39.590
You should all be quite familiar with this story...

02:47.060 --> 02:53.280
In the capital, in this period of peace under unified Toyotomi rule,

02:53.280 --> 02:56.990
one adventurer was about to rise up with fortune on his side.

03:12.050 --> 03:13.880
Excuse me!

03:12.210 --> 03:14.720
Yoshioka Dojo

03:15.300 --> 03:17.010
What business do you have here?

03:18.430 --> 03:21.930
...Musashi, I will bring my elder brother's vengeance upon you!

03:24.310 --> 03:27.730
We shall battle by the drooping pine at Ichijoji!

03:27.060 --> 03:28.690
Challenge

04:10.480 --> 04:11.940
He's late...

04:11.940 --> 04:13.520
You're late, Musashi!

04:22.660 --> 04:23.740
It's Musashi!

04:23.740 --> 04:25.700
Musashi is here!

04:43.600 --> 04:47.310
So you came, Musashi, like a moth to the flame!

04:47.310 --> 04:50.600
Men! Vengeance for my brother is there for the taking!

04:50.600 --> 04:51.980
Now!

05:18.210 --> 05:20.720
Musashi, did you come alone?

05:20.970 --> 05:22.760
Yep, just me.

05:22.760 --> 05:24.180
Are you a fool?

05:24.180 --> 05:26.970
Who knows, Denshichiro-dono.

05:26.970 --> 05:31.480
I do enjoy taking on lots of enemies by myself...

05:32.020 --> 05:33.650
...and winning!

05:44.700 --> 05:46.830
This is a sleep bullet.

05:46.830 --> 05:49.450
It can send someone to sleep for an hour.

05:49.450 --> 05:51.290
Sleep bullets, huh?

05:51.290 --> 05:55.040
You have any swords that work without killing?

05:55.040 --> 05:57.040
Ah, yes...

05:57.040 --> 06:01.380
I have an electric sword that can simply knock people out.

06:06.550 --> 06:07.720
What!?

06:07.720 --> 06:09.640
Revolvers? What a dirty trick!

06:09.970 --> 06:12.560
There are no "dirty tricks" in a battle.

06:12.560 --> 06:16.690
Anyway, I don't have time to waste on these boring fights.

06:17.110 --> 06:18.610
I want to get this over with.

06:18.860 --> 06:19.280
B- Boring!?

06:20.860 --> 06:25.160
You call it boring for two warriors to cross swords and do battle?

06:25.160 --> 06:28.410
Yep, it's completely boring, to me.

06:29.580 --> 06:33.330
I have way more important things to do!

06:33.330 --> 06:35.040
Like what?

06:39.840 --> 06:42.010
Castle-taking!

06:42.010 --> 06:43.760
What!?

06:43.760 --> 06:45.640
Capturing castles!

06:45.640 --> 06:50.930
Why don't you give it a try too, instead of sticking with that weak swordfighting?

06:50.930 --> 06:53.180
It's pretty fun!

06:53.180 --> 06:54.350
Upstart!

06:54.350 --> 06:55.900
You would insult the warrior's way!?

06:55.900 --> 07:00.400
If you have a scrap of chivalry within you, you should be ashamed of such banditry!

07:00.400 --> 07:03.280
You sure are hardheaded, for a young guy like you.

07:03.280 --> 07:04.820
Oho, is that so?

07:04.820 --> 07:06.320
Babble on...

07:06.320 --> 07:07.780
...all you want!

07:13.830 --> 07:14.460
Wh- Wha!?

07:40.980 --> 07:42.940
Why, you—

07:53.620 --> 07:55.250
Where do you want to get shot?

07:56.210 --> 07:57.870
Right or left?

07:57.870 --> 07:59.670
Head or stomach?

07:59.670 --> 08:01.840
Well, then...

08:01.840 --> 08:03.380
Stomach!

08:18.890 --> 08:22.310
There's Osaka for you, the Toyotomi headquarters.

08:23.400 --> 08:26.610
Musashi-dono, I urge you to reconsider.

08:26.610 --> 08:30.490
You again? You're persistent, Danjo-san.

08:31.120 --> 08:33.330
How many times have I said no by now?

08:33.330 --> 08:35.330
But the castle—

08:35.330 --> 08:37.620
Come on, give up!

08:37.620 --> 08:42.250
No one is more suitable than you to protect the princess!

08:42.250 --> 08:43.750
What are you talking about?

08:43.750 --> 08:46.050
You're doing a nice job yourself, Danjo-san.

08:46.050 --> 08:47.380
And that princess is...

08:47.380 --> 08:48.590
However...!

08:49.130 --> 08:50.510
In the first place,

08:50.510 --> 08:54.430
isn't it weird to ask a castle-taker like me to protect a castle?

08:54.430 --> 08:56.020
It just isn't right.

08:56.020 --> 09:02.980
It is precisely because you have conquered over thirty castles by now that I request this of you!

09:02.980 --> 09:05.070
Anyway, my answer's still no.

09:05.070 --> 09:07.280
I'm sorry, but pass that on to the princess, will you?

09:07.280 --> 09:08.490
Musashi-dono!

09:08.490 --> 09:12.110
They may be assaulting the castle again at this very moment!

09:12.110 --> 09:14.660
If you would please lend us your strength!

09:36.720 --> 09:38.310
Princess.

09:38.890 --> 09:39.890
Danjo?

09:40.140 --> 09:40.850
Yes.

09:41.730 --> 09:43.190
How went it?

09:43.940 --> 09:45.940
Excuse me.

09:46.770 --> 09:48.980
Did you meet him?

09:49.400 --> 09:54.950
My deepest apologies. I was unable to persuade him.

09:54.950 --> 09:57.540
Did I not say it?

09:57.870 --> 10:02.160
The man called Musashi could bring us success,

10:02.160 --> 10:05.840
but he will surely refuse.

10:05.840 --> 10:06.670
Yes.

10:07.500 --> 10:12.720
However, the time will come when Miyamoto Musashi's power shall become necessary.

10:12.720 --> 10:17.260
We must have him to overcome the <i>ayakashi</i>.

10:18.180 --> 10:21.980
Goodness, we have entered a strange world.

10:21.980 --> 10:26.060
Thanks to our Western Army's victory at the Battle of Sekigahara,

10:26.060 --> 10:30.610
we have finally achieved the deepest wish of our late regent Toyotomi Hideyoshi-sama

10:30.610 --> 10:33.530
and established Toyotomi sovereignty, but now this happens...

10:33.900 --> 10:39.490
It was just after the war that the ayakashi began to appear in this world.

10:40.330 --> 10:44.460
Could it be that the defeated Tokugawa have sent the ayakashi?

10:51.590 --> 10:57.300
I do not know. That may be the case, or it may not be.

10:57.890 --> 10:59.850
The moon is full tonight.

10:59.850 --> 11:03.270
Tighten the guard of the castle.

11:03.270 --> 11:06.350
Of course. The preparations have been taken care of.

11:19.700 --> 11:22.490
But still,

11:22.490 --> 11:25.250
things have taken a troublesome turn.

11:27.420 --> 11:29.000
Musashi-dono, is it?

11:29.000 --> 11:30.130
'Sup?

11:30.500 --> 11:33.960
What a coincidence this is.

11:34.340 --> 11:37.180
It's been a while, Ronin-dono.

11:39.890 --> 11:41.060
You have a job?

11:41.060 --> 11:42.010
Yep.

11:42.640 --> 11:44.810
Which castle will you take next?

11:45.680 --> 11:46.770
That one.

11:47.140 --> 11:49.860
It's finally come to this? Osaka Castle.

11:49.860 --> 11:51.570
The stronghold of the shogunate.

11:51.570 --> 11:53.780
Have you finished preparing?

11:53.780 --> 11:54.940
Nope.

11:54.940 --> 11:56.360
What?

11:56.360 --> 11:57.610
Oh, well.

11:57.610 --> 12:00.240
If there's time, we can come up with a plan.

12:00.240 --> 12:01.780
So, when are you doing it?

12:01.780 --> 12:02.910
Tonight.

12:02.910 --> 12:03.910
What are you—

12:03.910 --> 12:07.410
You're going to enter the castle of the shogunate without any preparation?

12:07.410 --> 12:08.960
Have you lost your mind?

12:08.960 --> 12:10.420
Well...

12:10.420 --> 12:14.880
I didn't expect I'd be going after it until later,

12:14.880 --> 12:17.510
but it's just so annoying.

12:17.510 --> 12:20.050
Annoying? What is?

12:20.050 --> 12:23.060
It's annoying for someone else to take

12:23.060 --> 12:26.350
what you've marked as your own prey!

12:26.350 --> 12:27.480
What?

12:27.480 --> 12:32.110
So tonight, someone <i>else</i> is going to
try to seize the castle...

12:32.110 --> 12:32.940
Really?

12:32.940 --> 12:34.650
No doubt about it.

12:34.650 --> 12:38.110
The conditions are perfect for an attack tonight.

12:38.110 --> 12:40.490
Who could this other castle-taker be?

12:40.490 --> 12:42.410
Sasaki Kojiro, it must be?

12:42.410 --> 12:47.870
Ronin! How many times have I told you not to say that name in front of me?

12:47.870 --> 12:51.880
I know! I know! You didn't like Kojiro's name!

12:51.880 --> 12:53.380
You said it again!

12:53.000 --> 12:55.420
- I'm sorry! Sorry!

12:56.510 --> 12:58.720
Don't say it again, Ronin.

12:59.430 --> 13:01.800
Thought I was going to die...

13:02.180 --> 13:04.850
But anyway, regardless of your skill,

13:04.850 --> 13:09.520
Osaka Castle is currently occupied by the Toyotomi clan.

13:09.520 --> 13:11.310
Taking it will be quite difficult.

13:11.310 --> 13:12.650
Of course it will.

13:16.360 --> 13:18.240
So, who is it?

13:18.240 --> 13:21.110
No human alive would try to seize Osaka Castle.

13:42.090 --> 13:43.680
They aren't human.

13:44.090 --> 13:46.430
Then the spirit realm? Ayakashi!?

14:05.030 --> 14:08.450
I won't let the ayakashi take it.

14:27.680 --> 14:28.930
No irregularities?

14:28.930 --> 14:30.180
None.

14:30.890 --> 14:33.600
Understood? Do not let even a single mouse in.

14:33.600 --> 14:34.190
Yes!

14:44.030 --> 14:48.280
Those ominous clouds, and this moon...

14:48.700 --> 14:51.700
Red, the color of blood.

14:52.960 --> 14:54.120
Princess.

15:16.400 --> 15:18.360
So here you are.

15:42.920 --> 15:44.720
Come at me!

15:45.970 --> 15:49.010
All of you will meet the same end.

16:09.110 --> 16:10.910
Splendid.

16:10.910 --> 16:12.660
As expected of you.

16:13.370 --> 16:15.830
You have improved.

16:18.420 --> 16:23.800
Tonight, I will not hold back as I did before.

16:31.050 --> 16:32.260
Yasha!

16:48.900 --> 16:52.990
A mere human cannot cut me.

16:53.450 --> 16:54.120
Wh- What!?

16:55.410 --> 16:56.790
What!?

16:56.790 --> 16:59.670
I thought that might be the case!

16:59.670 --> 17:02.460
How about this, then?

17:07.970 --> 17:09.470
Oh?

17:09.470 --> 17:12.010
You use an <i>onmyouken</i>?

17:12.010 --> 17:14.470
How will it be this time?

17:18.680 --> 17:21.770
So he is no ordinary samurai?

17:22.400 --> 17:23.770
Perhaps.

17:23.770 --> 17:27.150
Then I will treat you as such.

17:33.700 --> 17:35.330
Princess!

17:35.330 --> 17:36.830
Curses!

17:36.830 --> 17:37.910
Silence!

17:39.200 --> 17:41.710
You will remain quiet.

17:41.920 --> 17:45.000
You! What did you do? I can't move!

17:45.000 --> 17:48.960
Ryougen-sama is waiting. Resign yourself to it.

17:48.960 --> 17:51.800
I will not become the bride of an ayakashi!

17:54.220 --> 17:56.390
I'll be taking your princess.

17:57.260 --> 17:59.430
No! Return her!

18:04.810 --> 18:07.520
Return her! Bring her back!

18:13.410 --> 18:15.450
What happened to the guards?

18:16.370 --> 18:20.370
A carriage here in the forest, and ayakashi.

18:20.370 --> 18:22.210
There must be something up.

18:22.210 --> 18:23.960
And yet...

18:24.460 --> 18:28.090
While I heard an ayakashi was going to take the castle,

18:28.090 --> 18:31.510
your only target was the princess?

18:31.510 --> 18:33.180
I didn't even have to come here.

18:34.130 --> 18:36.180
Where are my subordinates?

18:36.510 --> 18:38.390
They <i>left</i>.

18:38.760 --> 18:42.390
Is that so? It seems you're a bit capable.

18:42.390 --> 18:44.350
Well? Who are you?

18:44.350 --> 18:45.520
Musashi.

18:45.520 --> 18:47.810
My name is Miyamoto Musashi!

18:47.810 --> 18:50.030
Miyamoto Musashi...

18:50.030 --> 18:51.440
I have not heard of you.

18:51.440 --> 18:53.650
I am Ronin.

19:00.160 --> 19:02.660
Can you stop me?

19:03.290 --> 19:05.960
Hm, I wonder.

19:05.960 --> 19:07.670
Shall I give it a try?

19:14.300 --> 19:16.340
Let us begin.

19:17.470 --> 19:20.350
I see you also have strange sword technique.

19:20.350 --> 19:22.930
What is its name?

19:22.930 --> 19:25.600
<i>Nenken: Meiretsu</i>.

19:28.650 --> 19:30.110
Too weak!

19:32.360 --> 19:33.610
What was that?

19:38.570 --> 19:40.950
Now things are interesting.

19:40.950 --> 19:43.790
This is tough. Let's do this, Musashi!

19:47.540 --> 19:48.960
What?

19:48.960 --> 19:50.380
You...

19:50.380 --> 19:52.880
<i>Onmyoudan</i> bullets, designed for ayakashi.

19:52.880 --> 19:56.050
I talked an old inventor into selling them to me.

19:56.050 --> 19:57.760
Guess they work pretty well.

20:19.870 --> 20:20.820
Not good enough!

20:21.870 --> 20:23.290
Take this!

20:28.960 --> 20:30.710
Ow!

20:47.350 --> 20:48.640
The final blow!

20:53.190 --> 20:54.020
What!?

20:54.270 --> 20:57.110
I got this for Musashi. <i>Danpasen</i>.

20:57.110 --> 20:58.030
Here I come!

21:04.240 --> 21:06.040
Quite impressive.

21:06.040 --> 21:09.500
But not on the level of Sasaki Kojiro!

21:10.830 --> 21:13.290
Don't say that name!

21:14.590 --> 21:17.800
I hate that name!

21:17.800 --> 21:21.510
I, Gundoh Musashi, will not let ayakashi like you have your way!

21:32.400 --> 21:33.860
Curses...

21:34.480 --> 21:37.940
I will relinquish this battle.

21:37.940 --> 21:39.150
Farewell!

21:40.990 --> 21:43.570
Feels like we barely won.

21:43.570 --> 21:46.700
Yeah. He was really strong.

21:47.660 --> 21:50.540
Now, what to do about this unruly princess?

21:50.540 --> 21:53.250
Leave her alone. Danjo's here.

21:53.250 --> 21:54.960
Princess Kaguya!

21:54.960 --> 21:56.290
Princess!

21:58.380 --> 21:59.550
See?

21:59.550 --> 22:00.800
So he is.

22:17.730 --> 22:20.650
Musashi. I've finally found you.

22:20.650 --> 22:22.820
I'll kill you this time!

22:22.820 --> 22:25.990
No point, you know. Just give up.

22:26.320 --> 22:27.870
He found me?

22:27.870 --> 22:30.950
My aim is flawless! I won't miss!

22:30.950 --> 22:34.120
Women are stubborn no matter what country they're from.

22:34.120 --> 22:37.960
Don't look down on me, the great Desperado!

22:39.300 --> 22:42.010
I don't fight women!

22:42.010 --> 22:43.880
Why do you keep following me?

22:43.880 --> 22:47.430
I hate this! He ran away again!

22:47.930 --> 22:49.930
Don't run!

22:50.310 --> 22:55.350
Stupid, of course I'm gonna run!

23:02.610 --> 23:05.610
Last night, how did I...

23:05.610 --> 23:08.070
You don't remember?

23:08.530 --> 23:12.040
I was unable to protect you.

23:12.040 --> 23:14.330
I am deeply sorry.

23:14.750 --> 23:17.380
Miyamoto Musashi...

23:17.960 --> 23:19.960
I'm sure that Musashi-dono...

23:20.590 --> 23:22.960
I can tell.

23:22.960 --> 23:28.890
He... Musashi-dono was the one who saved me.

23:32.270 --> 23:35.690
Musashi. Which castle will you take next?

23:35.690 --> 23:37.440
The castle of the ayakashi.

23:37.440 --> 23:39.520
But first...

23:39.520 --> 23:40.860
First?

23:41.690 --> 23:43.740
I'll need training.

23:43.740 --> 23:45.570
They're strong.

23:45.990 --> 23:48.570
And I owe Yasha some payback.

23:49.530 --> 23:51.120
Miyamoto Musashi...

23:51.120 --> 23:52.790
I will remember you.

23:54.080 --> 23:55.790
Just you wait!

24:00.590 --> 24:03.340
In my natural, unadorned style,

24:03.340 --> 24:06.170
I'll tell you these feelings of mine

24:06.170 --> 24:11.510
Together to the sky past the darkness!

24:11.510 --> 24:16.640
All we need to do is spread our wings and fly!

24:18.190 --> 24:23.320
Baby, we'll send time flowing forward just a little,

24:23.320 --> 24:29.490
and we'll embrace even the harsh gusts of wind

24:29.490 --> 24:34.830
with sympathy for pointless worries

24:34.830 --> 24:38.960
and a melody that will overcome the pain

24:41.330 --> 24:51.720
If the poison of the flower that bloomed in my cupped hands

24:51.720 --> 25:02.650
has managed to pierce through the center of my heart...

25:02.650 --> 25:05.400
In my natural, unadorned style,

25:05.400 --> 25:08.280
I'll tell you these feelings of mine,

25:08.280 --> 25:13.870
Unraveling this puzzle of the heart

25:13.870 --> 25:16.620
I'll bring out every part

25:16.620 --> 25:19.620
of your unchanging style

25:19.620 --> 25:24.920
Together to the sky past the darkness!

25:24.920 --> 25:30.090
All we need to do is spread our wings and fly!

25:31.970 --> 25:34.430
Time for training!

25:34.850 --> 25:37.850
I will master <i>gun-dou<i>!</i></i>

25:39.180 --> 25:44.060
The next chapter: <i>Gun-dou</i>!
